cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FP127, FP19 or BlockulatorWad, please cite it as below."
title: "Blockulator: FP127 and FP19, high-precision math for the EVM"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Secure Data Research, LLC"
    website: "https://securedataresearch.net"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/securedataresearch/blockulator"
url: "https://blockulator.com"
abstract: >-
  Three math libraries for the EVM in which every op is exact or rounds once.
  FP127 is signed 127.128 fixed point: 38 digits at 1 and a range of
  ±1.7 × 10^38, in 53 ops. FP19 is a 256-bit binary float: about 71 digits at
  any magnitude from 10^-78,913 to 10^78,913, in 65 ops, the special
  functions among them. BlockulatorWad keeps Solady's WAD function names and
  signatures and returns the exact value rounded once in the stated direction.
  FP127 and FP19 ship as deployed contracts with no owner and as inline
  libraries; BlockulatorWad is inline only.
version: "3.0"
date-released: "2026-10-28"
keywords:
  - ethereum
  - evm
  - fixed-point
  - floating-point
  - solidity
  - yul
